 "notes": "Same GPIO wiring as gray-a. The map is separate because the IP5306 is not on I2C in this revision: the Gray changelog's 2017.12 entry connects it to the I2C bus. The Gray page does not state whether the unit has PSRAM; it lists G16/G17 as base-interface pins with no other use, so they carry no use here and the SoC's PSRAM caution applies. Port A is the internal I2C bus (G21/G22); the revision's components say which chips sit on it. The unit has one Grove port, Port A. The pages' HY2.0-4P table also gives Port B (G26/G36) and Port C (G17/G16), the pins a base with those ports uses; here they reach only the M-Bus. Buttons A/B/C sit on input-only G39/G38/G37 and reach no connector, so they are marked fixed: no feature can be switched off to free them.",
